The Go rendering: an application declaring one iota group per way a value of
the type arises by no member's name (a range over a member, a generic helper, a
function iterator, a decoder taking the destination as any, called directly or
through a variable, a slice or a field of any, a conversion between pointer
types, reflection, a type switch, a channel handed to outside code), each group
naming its first and third member and no other. Two variables hold a decoder a
test file installs. The YAML, TOML and outside modules are local modules the
target requires and replaces, so the rendering loads with no network access.

